#, no-c-format
msgid "A Typical DAM Workflow"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-dam-workflow.docbook:6
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Import images from camera, card reader or scanner. As long as the images are "
"stored on the camera media, you can use that as temporary backup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-dam-workflow.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid "RAW are converted to DNG and stored away into an RAW archive."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-dam-workflow.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid "Rate and cull, write-back metadata to the DNG archive."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-dam-workflow.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid "Make a backup &eg; on external drive, and optical medium, or a tape."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-dam-workflow.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tag, comment, and geo-locate."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-dam-workflow.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid "Edit and improve photographs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-dam-workflow.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For layered editing use external applications. Back in &digikam;, re-apply "
"the metadata, which was probably lost or curtailed by the other applications."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-dam-workflow.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid "Run the routine backup with following data-integrity checks"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-dam-workflow.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Protect processed images for copyrights with Digital Watermarking. Export to "
"web galleries, slide shows, MPEG encode, contact sheets, printing &etc;"
msgstr ""

